# Mac node environment configuration (browser automation, computer use,
# heavier local models, coding/desktop execution).
#
# Copy to ~/.hermes/.env on the Mac (mode 0600). Fill in real values. Never
# commit a populated copy of this file.
#
# The Mac may be offline without breaking Titan — Titan degrades gracefully
# (see deploy/titan/README.md and scripts/fleet_connectivity_check.py) and
# returns a clear deferred/unavailable result for Mac-only work rather than
# hanging or silently failing.
#
# This file documents ONLY what is specific to the Mac's role. The full
# canonical list of every environment variable Hermes understands lives in
# the repository root's .env.example.

# ── GitHub (source of truth) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Hermes Link (Mac/Titan governed communication) ───────────────────────
# The Mac acts as the coordinator (big_sister) — it holds no service token
# of its own; instead it authenticates *to* Titan using the same token
# Titan's HERMES_LINK_TOKEN was set to (or the signed-registry path — see
# deploy/mac/README.md).
HERMES_LINK_TOKEN=
# Reachable-over-Tailscale base URL for Titan's tunneled Hermes Link port
# (see deploy/mac/README.md for the tunnel setup this depends on).
HERMES_LINK_TITAN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:19320

# ── Computer use (macOS desktop control) ──────────────────────────────────
# No credential required, but requires Accessibility + Screen Recording
# permissions granted to the terminal/app running Hermes. Run
# `hermes computer_use doctor` after granting to confirm.

# ── Browser automation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Chromium mode needs no credentials. Cloud modes are optional:
# BROWSERBASE_API_KEY=
# BROWSERBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# BROWSER_USE_API_KEY=

# ── Local models (Ollama) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Heavier local models run on the Mac per the target architecture. No
# Hermes-side credential needed for a local Ollama endpoint; ensure Ollama
# itself is installed and the desired models are pulled.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# ── Terminal tool backend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
TERMINAL_ENV=local
